' PAL — State diagram for UC-09: Booking cancellation paths + Refund substate
@startuml PAL_State_UC09_Booking_Cancellation

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #444
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #FDF6E3
skinparam StateBorderColor #333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #888
hide empty description

title UC-09 — Booking state machine (cancellation focus) with Refund substate

' ====== Top-level states (declared explicitly) ======
state PaidPickupPending
state Active
state "RentalRequest.Approved\n(anchor from UC-05;\nno Booking exists yet)" as ExtApproved
state "to dispute (UC-09 alt 1a)" as DisputeExit

' ====== Composite: Cancelled (refund substates) ======
state Cancelled {
  [*] --> Refunding : / issue refund via gateway\n(amount per cancellation policy)
  Refunding --> RefundSettled : gateway confirms refund
  Refunding --> RefundPending : gateway failure (alt 6a)\n/ mark reconcile async
  RefundPending --> RefundSettled : async reconciliation succeeds
  RefundPending : do / retry reconciliation
  RefundSettled --> [*]
}

' ====== Booking transitions into cancellation ======
[*] --> PaidPickupPending : Booking entered from UC-06

PaidPickupPending --> Cancelled : user cancels, pickup in future\n/ free slot, notify other party
PaidPickupPending --> DisputeExit : pickup time already in past\n/ Cancel disabled, suggest dispute
Active            --> Cancelled : dispute resolution cancels\nan active booking (rare)
ExtApproved      --> Cancelled : (cross-UC, from UC-05.Approved)\nuser cancels before paying\n/ no refund needed (no charge yet)

DisputeExit --> [*]

note right of Cancelled
  Cancellation policy (placeholders, flagged
  as assumptions, see UC-09 step 3):
   * more than 24h before pickup : 100% refund
   * 6 to 24h before pickup      :  50% refund
   * less than 6h before pickup  :   0% refund
  Exact percentages are configurable and not
  fixed in the spec.
end note

note left of DisputeExit
  UC-09 alt 1a: when the pickup time has
  already passed, the Cancel option is
  disabled and the system suggests opening
  a dispute instead. Modelled here as a
  pseudo-terminal exit, not a real Cancelled
  Booking state.
end note

note bottom
  Source: UC-09. Diagram is complementary to
  UC-07; only the Booking states that participate
  in cancellation are shown. The "cancel before
  payment" edge originates outside the Booking
  lifecycle (RentalRequest.Approved in UC-05).

  Operational (non-enum) substates inside Cancelled,
  introduced per state_plan.md to model the Refund
  machine: Refunding, RefundSettled, RefundPending
  (alt 6a).
end note

@enduml
